# Example crontab for the equities data platform.
# Install with:  crontab -e   and paste (adjusting the path).
#
# Times are in the host's local time; the entries below assume US/Eastern so
# the daily refresh runs after the market close and after Stooq's EOD files
# settle. Adjust if your host runs UTC (add ~5 hours in winter, 4 in summer).
#
# run_job.sh handles venv activation, .env loading, and per-run log files in
# data/logs/, so the entries stay one line each.

PLATFORM=/opt/equities_data_platform

# Securities master + EOD prices + latest filings: 22:30 ET every weekday.
30 22 * * 1-5  $PLATFORM/scripts/run_job.sh daily-refresh

# Fundamentals (XBRL company facts) + 13F holdings: 03:00 ET on the 1st and
# 15th of each month -- SEC quarterly data trickles in around filing deadlines,
# so twice a month keeps fundamentals fresh without hammering the API.
0 3 1,15 * *   $PLATFORM/scripts/run_job.sh quarterly-refresh

# Optional: weekly deep price backfill (fills gaps, new listings' history):
# 0 4 * * 6    $PLATFORM/scripts/run_job.sh backfill --start 2000-01-01
